  "text": "Recipe: Dahi Vada (Baked)\nCreator: Sharmila Vedam\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: split black gram dal (urad dal; skinless), green chilies, ginger, onion, salt, baking soda, hing (asafetida), chili powder, soy yogurt, Tamarind Chutney, cumin powder, Green Chutney, cilantro\nCooking methods: bake, no-cook\nInstructions: BATTER: Soak 1 cup of split black gram dal (urad dal; skinless) for 1 hour. Grind soaked dal into a smooth dough along with green chilies & ginger (to taste). Added finely chopped onion (to taste; approximately 1 cup), salt (to taste) and 1/4 tsp baking soda. BAKING: Bake in silicon donut mould to prepare Vadas. I usually bake for 20-30 mins at 375F. HOT WATER SOAK: After baking, immerse the vadas in hot water for 10 minutes. I added hing (asafetida) & chili powder to hot water. After soaking, squeeze out most of the water. SERVE: Arrange the vadas in a serving bowl. Add beaten soy yogurt, Tamarind Chutney, chili powder, crushed roasted cumin powder, Green Chutney & chopped cilantro.\nNotes: Vadas are prepared using a silicon donut mould.",
